  "body": "What happens: opening a project resets the open document before the new file is parsed. A `.camproj` that is valid text but bad JSON (or otherwise fails to load) therefore leaves the user with an empty document: the old one is gone and the new one did not load. Only a non-text file is refused before the reset. Both paths do it: the disk open and the browser byte open (`open_project_bytes`, PR 1314).\n\nExpected: a project that cannot be loaded changes nothing. Parse and check the new file first; replace the open document only when the load succeeded.\n\nEvidence: found by reading in the review of PR 1314 (its body says a refused project \"changes nothing\", which holds for a non-text file only). Not reproduced by running the app.\n\nPriority note: rated P3 because Open replaces the document anyway when it succeeds; raise it if unsaved work is lost without the unsaved-changes prompt.\n\nDone means: a test opens a corrupt project over a document with content, on the disk path and the byte path, and the document, its history and its file name are unchanged; the refusal names the file.\n",
